%% Build spectrum — Ways to Build & Deliver Apps.
%% Decision flow: already have an image? -> no image, have source -> S2I or a Containerfile,
%% depending on whether you need control of the base image and build steps -> once the build
%% belongs to the team (every push: test, scan, sign), it moves into a pipeline. Node order and
%% wording follow concept.adoc's "Two build strategies — and where pipelines fit" verbatim.
%% Resized 2026-08-22: graph TD (524x1259, text at 1.72x) -> flowchart LR. A spectrum reads
%% left-to-right, so flipping direction is the fix; also merged two 3-line labels (Q2, Q3) down
%% to 2 lines each by removing a line break, not a word.
%% Corrected 2026-08-23: that last step overshot — measured 900x241 at 0.43x text, i.e. ~2100px
%% intrinsic, unreadably small once the 900px cap scales it down. In an LR diagram each rank is as
%% wide as its widest LABEL LINE, and this one's aspect was 0.27, so height was free and width was
%% not: Q2, Q3 and PIPE went BACK to three lines and START to two. No NODE label lost a word, and
%% the six ranks are unchanged — concept.adoc's decision order is the lesson. One edge label did
%% change: `No, just build it` on Q2->S2I became `No`, because an edge label sets rank SEPARATION
%% in LR and the question it answers is right above it.
%% Still around 1400px afterwards rather than inside the 750-1100 band. Closing that last gap means
%% dropping a rank, and every one of the six is a step concept.adoc walks in order.
flowchart LR
  START([You have<br/>an app to run]) --> Q1{Do you already<br/>have an image?}
  Q1 -->|Yes| DEPLOY[Deploy from image<br/>no build]
  Q1 -->|No, I have source| Q2{Do you need control<br/>of the base image<br/>and build steps?}
  Q2 -->|No| S2I[Import from Git<br/>Source-to-Image]
  Q2 -->|Yes| DOCKER[Containerfile build<br/>Buildah]
  S2I --> Q3{Does the build belong<br/>to the team now?<br/>every push, test, scan, sign}
  DOCKER --> Q3
  Q3 -->|Yes| PIPE["Run the same build<br/>from a Pipeline<br/>(separate module)"]
  Q3 -->|Not yet| DONE([Running app])
  DEPLOY --> DONE
  classDef pick fill:#e00,stroke:#900,color:#fff;
  class DEPLOY,S2I,DOCKER pick;
  classDef later fill:#fff,stroke:#900,color:#900,stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  class PIPE later;
